{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>An archer (רֹבֶה קַשָּׁת).</b> Because קַשָּׁת is a noun of description, they said that רֹבֶה is the one who shoots arrows, from the language of \"my archers (רַבָּיו) surround me\" (Job 16:13), \"and they embittered him and shot (וָרֹבּוּ)\" (Genesis 49:23), and קַשָּׁת is the maker of bows. But it is more correct that רֹבֶה is the shooter, and it is said of one who shoots arrows and of one who hurls stones and the like, as one says \"which I shot (יָסֹבּוּ/יָרִיתִי) between me and you\" (Genesis 31:51). Therefore Scripture describes him another time as a קַשָּׁת, and likewise \"and the archers (הַמּוֹרִים), men who drew the bow (בַּקָּשֶׁת), found him\" (I Samuel 31:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The verse citations in the Hebrew appear slightly garbled in places (e.g., Job 16:13 is cited as איוב טז יג without standard punctuation; I Samuel 31:3 is cited as שמואל א לא ג); these have been rendered as standard English verse references. The root יסב/ירה conflation in the Job and Genesis citations is translated according to the standard text of each verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:52.172768926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}